{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno3_js_face_recon",
    "description": "Pointwise classical (Jiang-Shu 1996) WENO3 reconstruction of a cell-averaged/point field at the face between the second and third cells of a three-cell window v0, v1, v2 (cells i-1, i, i+1 for the face i+1/2, upwind-biased to the left): the two second-order candidate stencils p0 = (-v0 + 3 v1)/2 on {i-1, i} and p1 = (v1 + v2)/2 on {i, i+1}, linear weights gamma0 = 1/3 and gamma1 = 2/3 (whose linear combination is the third-order upwind-biased reconstruction (-v0 + 5 v1 + 2 v2)/6), smoothness indicators beta0 = (v1 - v0)^2, beta1 = (v2 - v1)^2, and the CLASSICAL nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2 with eps = 1e-6 and power 2. It is the third-order sibling of stencils/weno5_js_face_recon on this grid, with the same weight construction, the same eps and the same orientation, and it is NOT the same scheme as grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/stencils/weno3_recon: that one is WENO-Z (Borges 2008), whose weights are alpha_k = gamma_k (1 + (tau3/(eps + beta_k))^2) with the global smoothness measure tau3 = |beta0 - beta1|. The two agree only where the field is smooth; across a kink they weight the sub-stencils differently, so they must not be substituted for one another. eps = 1e-6 is the literal fire_behavior uses (TOL in Select_weno3), on the field's own value scale; it is not dimensionally scaled. Third order in smooth regions, degrading to the non-oscillatory single-stencil value across a discontinuity. Match-less helper of the weno3_eno1_* stencils of this grid; the mirrored (right-biased) face is obtained by binding the window in reverse order.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:reconstruct",
      "axes:x",
      "order:3",
      "stencil_width:3"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Shu, C.-W. (1996). Efficient implementation of weighted ENO schemes. Journal of Computational Physics, 126(1), 202-228. The classical WENO smoothness indicators beta_k and nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2, specialised here to the two-stencil third-order window.",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1996.0130"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Select_weno3 (and Calc_tend_ls cases 6 and 8). The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
